---
# qlib 的静态分析门禁，针对 clang-tidy 23 验证（见 CI）。
# Static analysis gate for qlib, verified against clang-tidy 23 (see CI).
#
# 继承关系：tests/ 与 fuzz/ 都继承本文件，各自关闭一两个对它们不适用的检查——
# 见 tests/.clang-tidy 与 fuzz/.clang-tidy。理由写在那两个文件里，而不是这里，
# 因为它们只在那些目录里成立。
# tests/ and fuzz/ inherit this file and each disable one or two checks that do
# not apply to them -- see tests/.clang-tidy and fuzz/.clang-tidy. The reasons live
# there rather than here, because they are only true in those directories.
#
# 启用的模块：bugprone、cert、clang-analyzer、misc、performance、portability、
# readability。这里不启用 modernize / cppcoreguidelines / abseil：它们写的是 C++
# 规则，而这个库的构建参数是 -std=c11 加 C_EXTENSIONS OFF，一条 C++ 建议在这里
# 要么无意义，要么会把代码推向本库刻意回避的方向。
# Enabled modules: bugprone, cert, clang-analyzer, misc, performance, portability,
# readability. modernize, cppcoreguidelines and abseil are not enabled: they encode
# C++ rules, and this library builds as -std=c11 with C_EXTENSIONS off. A C++-only
# suggestion here is either meaningless or pushes the code in a direction the
# library deliberately avoids.
#
# 刻意关闭的检查，每一条都有具体理由：
# Checks deliberately disabled, each for a concrete reason:
#
#   -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters：在统一的 (ptr, size, userdata) 分配器
#     回调签名下无法避免。
#   -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters: unavoidable with the uniform
#     (ptr, size, userdata) allocator callback signature.
#
#   -readability-magic-numbers：位运算和数学代码里噪声太大。
#   -readability-magic-numbers: noisy for bit manipulation and math code.
#
#   -readability-identifier-length：要求局部变量至少 3 个字符，这与地道的 C
#     （n、i、p、ok）为敌。
#   -readability-identifier-length: demands >= 3 character locals, which is
#     hostile to idiomatic C (n, i, p, ok).
#
#   -readability-implicit-bool-conversion：在 C 里比较表达式产生 int，因此从一个
#     bool 函数写 `return a < b;` 就是一次隐式的 int -> bool 转换。这是正常的 C；
#     该检查是按 C++ 语义写的，它的 AllowIntegerConditions 只覆盖条件，不覆盖返回
#     值。
#   -readability-implicit-bool-conversion: in C a comparison yields int, so
#     `return a < b;` from a bool function is an implicit int -> bool
#     conversion. That is ordinary C; the check is written for C++ semantics
#     and its AllowIntegerConditions option only covers conditions, not returns.
#
#   -clang-analyzer-security.insecureAPI.DeprecatedOrUnsafeBufferHandling：它要求
#     改用 Annex K 的 *_s 函数（memcpy_s、memset_s……）。Annex K 是可选的，glibc
#     和 macOS libc 都不提供，照着做会让本库支持的三个平台里有两个坏掉。
#     memcpy/memset/memmove 才是这里正确的工具。
#   -clang-analyzer-security.insecureAPI.DeprecatedOrUnsafeBufferHandling: insists
#     on the Annex K *_s functions (memcpy_s, memset_s, ...). Annex K is optional
#     and glibc and macOS libc do not provide it, so following this advice would
#     break two of the three platforms we support. memcpy/memset/memmove are the
#     correct tools here.
#
#   -misc-include-cleaner：它要求每个符号都来自直接包含的头文件，也就是 IWYU。
#     对 C 项目它过于激进：qlib.h 是有意重导出的汇总头，而 size_t、uint32_t、
#     CLOCK_MONOTONIC 由 <stddef.h>/<stdint.h>/<time.h> 传递提供也是 C 的常规做法。
#     在本库上它会报 339 条，没有一条是缺陷。
#   -misc-include-cleaner: demands every symbol come from a directly included
#     header, which is IWYU. Too aggressive for a C project: qlib.h is a
#     deliberate re-exporting umbrella header, and it is ordinary C to get size_t,
#     uint32_t or CLOCK_MONOTONIC transitively. It reports 339 findings here and
#     none of them is a defect.
#
# 注意：注释必须留在 `Checks` 这个折叠块标量之外——YAML 在折叠块里把 '#' 当作内容，
# 写成注释会静默地污染列表。
# NOTE: comments must stay outside the `Checks` block scalar -- YAML treats '#' as
# content inside a folded block, which would silently corrupt the list.
Checks: >
  bugprone-*,
  cert-*,
  clang-analyzer-*,
  misc-*,
  performance-*,
  portability-*,
  readability-*,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  -readability-magic-numbers,
  -readability-identifier-length,
  -readability-implicit-bool-conversion,
  -clang-analyzer-security.insecureAPI.DeprecatedOrUnsafeBufferHandling,
  -misc-include-cleaner

# 只报告我们自己代码里的问题：不报系统头，也不报经由它们引入的第三方代码。
# 范围限定在 qlib 的公开头文件和测试头文件上。
# Report diagnostics from our own code only: not from system headers, nor from
# third party code pulled in through them. The scope is qlib's public headers and
# the test headers.
HeaderFilterRegex: '(include/qlib/|tests/).*\.h$'
SystemHeaders: false

# `--fix` 产生的代码按 .clang-format 排版，而不是 clang-tidy 的内置默认。没有这一
# 行，自动修复会产出与本项目风格不一致的代码，然后再被格式检查打回。
# Code produced by `--fix` is formatted with .clang-format rather than clang-tidy's
# built-in default. Without this, an autofix yields code in the wrong style that the
# format check then rejects.
FormatStyle: file

# 任何一条发现都会让 CI 失败。这条规则之所以成立，是因为"关闭的检查"上面都给了
# 理由：一个可以随手关掉的检查等于没有检查。
# Any finding fails the CI job. That is only workable because every disabled check
# above has a reason: a check that can be switched off casually is no check at all.
WarningsAsErrors: '*'
...
